    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.CurrentVersion">Current Running Version</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.ReleasedVersion">Released Version</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.LTSNotice">Thank you for using BedrockBoot 2.0, currently an LTS long-term support release.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.AbbrevNotice">Hereafter, BedrockBoot 2.0 is referred to as BedrockBoot.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.CrossPlatform">Cross-Platform Support</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.AvaloniaDesc">Thanks to the powerful Avalonia framework, BedrockBoot can now run on more operating systems.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.PlatformSupport">You can now use BedrockBoot on most x64 Windows and Linux operating systems to play Minecraft Bedrock.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.LinuxLimit">Currently, the Linux platform only supports GDK builds of Minecraft Bedrock due to game framework limitations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.LinuxLogin">On Linux, you can now log in to your account within the launcher and access it directly in-game for online play.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.Multiplayer">New Multiplayer Support</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.PaperConnect">Rebuilt communication logic with the PaperConnect v2 protocol, powered by the GravityCone multiplayer module.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.MoreFeatures">More Unique Features</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.ToolsDesc">You can now experience many features in the launcher's toolbox. For example: save conversion, resource pack conversion. These built-in tools can help you convert game assets, allowing for the conversion of resources between the Java and Bedrock editions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.ReleaseNotes.ResourceMgmt">You can even manage various in-game resources, such as: resource packs, behavior packs, skin packs, saves, and world templates...</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.Changelog.Title">Changelog</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="About.Changelog.Empty">No changelog available</x:String>
