    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.NoDumpFile">No dump file generated</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.NoExceptionReport">No exception report captured</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Phase.VEH">VEH Vector Exception Capture</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Phase.SEH">SEH Top-Level Filter Capture</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Phase.Manual">Manual Capture</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.NoStackTrace">Unable to retrieve call stack</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.NoReport">No crash report was generated for this abnormal exit, so no further analysis is available.&#x0a;To capture native exceptions, enable "Native Exception Capture" in instance settings, then reproduce the issue to obtain a complete analysis.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.NullPointer">The accessed address is close to 0, most likely a null pointer reference. This often happens when resources are not fully loaded or a mod is incompatible with the current game version.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.IllegalAccess">An illegal memory access occurred. Check modules outside the game itself in the call stack (mods, injected runtimes, drivers, etc.).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.StackOverflow">Thread stack space exhausted, often caused by infinite recursion or very large stack allocations. May be related to a faulty mod.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.FastFail">Runtime fast-fail: an unrecoverable internal error was detected, often caused by a mismatch between an injected runtime and the game version.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.Breakpoint">A breakpoint instruction was triggered, possibly an internal debug assertion in the game.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.ModCrash">The crash source {0} is a mod DLL in this instance's mod directory. This crash was most likely caused by that mod.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.ModCrash.Suggestion">Try disabling the mod in the instance's mod manager and reproduce to verify. Then check whether it is compatible with the current game version, or report it to the mod author with the exported crash report attached.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.ThirdParty">A third-party module {0} appeared in the call stack. Prioritize investigating mods or runtimes related to it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Analysis.Suggestion">Try self-repair based on the analysis above first. If that does not help, click "Export Crash Report" in the upper right to package it and ask others for help.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Export.Empty.Title">No Files to Export</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="CrashReport.Export.Empty.Message">No usable report or dump files for this crash</x:String>
